[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked **known**: one issue, one fix queued. It is not one issue.
The desk's own logic in `causes.ts` tells two causes apart, and the desk's notes name a third. The
table below is computed from the same export the incident page uses; nothing in it is typed in.

<Callout kind="warn">
Fixing the parser clears most of #4471, not all of it. Two smaller faults stay open until they get
their own fix.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<SplitTable ticket={4471} repo="MaciekZybura/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows" issues={{ parser: 1, hint: 2, 'one-day-move': 3 }} />

The export has 427 records but 412 reports: its pages overlap, so 15 reports come twice. Every
count here is over unique ids.

### parser · the queued fix

The shared parser reads every date month first. All eleven tenants on file write the day first,
so any day up to the 12th comes back with month and day swapped: 7 April becomes 4 July. Reports
reach us from every tenant and every channel. This is the fix already queued.

### hint · the booking-v3 form

The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People at the three booking-v3
tenants (alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour) type what the hint says, month first, and the
form reads it the tenant's way. Same symptom, different cause: the parser fix does not touch the
hint. Every one of these came through the form.

### one-day-move · not a month flip

Five reports describe a move of exactly one day: a Tuesday shown as the Monday, one meeting on two
days in Lisbon and Toronto, an invite that arrived before the booking. The desk read them as a
one-day move and footnoted them under `parser` by tenant. They are a time-zone or day-boundary
fault and had no ticket until now.

## Why the merge hid this

The desk merges on subject line alone
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). "Booking on the wrong date" from a
booking-v3 form and from the app share a subject and land in one ticket, though
[the dedupe explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe) shows they are different causes. Intake's `parser` and
`hint` tags are guesses from the reporter's browser locale: 23 `hint` tags sit on parser
reports and 15 `parser` tags on hint reports. The tenant's locale and form decide, not the browser.

## What to do

- Keep #4471 for `parser`; it covers most of the queue.
- Open the two other tickets (linked in the table) and move their reports out of #4471.
- When a report arrives, place it by tenant and channel with `causeOf`, not by intake tag.
- Re-read [the incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) after the parser fix ships: its "one issue" line
  will be wrong until then.

